    "content": {
      "value": "Requirements extracted from Zimmermann Functional Requirements excel, downloaded July 3rd, 2026 after all requirements were confirmed.. Req ID prefix: **DMU**.\n\n⚠️ **Rows with strikethrough are out of scope** — struck through in the Excel source file.\n\n| Req ID | Sub-Functional Area | Requirement | Owner | Config/Custom | Status | **Comments** | **User Story Link** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| DMU-001 | Data Migration | The system will receive all active product records via the AP21 to SFCC product feed through MuleSoft, including product names, descriptions, attributes, imagery references and category assignments, covering approximately 1,600 active SKUs at any point in time | Mule Integrator | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3DDMU-001> |\n| DMU-002 | Data Migration | ~~The system will use AP21 as the master of record for all product data post-migration, consuming ongoing product synchronisation into SFCC via MuleSoft.~~  The system will consume ongoing product data synchronisation into SFCC via MuleSoft, treating the downstream systems as the authoritative source of record for all product data post-migration. | Accenture | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-002> |\n| DMU-003 | Data Migration | The system will preserve multi-region product catalogue assignments and regional merchandising configurations across all storefronts. | Accenture | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-003> |\n| DMU-004 | Data Migration | ~~The system will migrate all registered customer account records, including name, phone number, email address, all saved delivery addresses (no limit on the number of addresses per account), and communication preferences.~~  The system will migrate customer email address and Omneo ID only. All other customer data including name, phone number, saved delivery addresses and communication preferences will be sourced live from Omneo at login. | Mule Integrator | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-004> |\n| DMU-005 | Data Migration | The system will not migrate customer passwords; customers will be required to reset their password on first login to the new platform. | Dependent SF Functionlity | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-005> |\n| DMU-006 | Data Migration | The system will not migrate saved payment card details; customers will be required to re-enter payment information at next purchase after go-live. | Dependent SF Functionlity | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-006> |\n| DMU-007 | Data Migration | The system will not migrate historical order records into SFCC; order history will be accessible ~~via NewStor~~e via Mulesoft where customer identifiers match across online and in-store channels. | Dependent SF Functionlity | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-007> |\n| DMU-008 | Data Migration | The system will display online orders only in the My Account order history for the Middle East storefront; offline and retail orders will not be surfaced. | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-008> |\n| DMU-009 | Data Migration | The system will reconfigure existing Contentful API connections to point to the new commerce platform; no bulk content re-entry will be required for content already managed in Contentful. | Accenture | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-009> |\n| ~~DMU-010~~ | Data Migration | ~~The system will migrate product images and digital assets to the new platform CDN, updating image URLs accordingly and applying 301 redirects where asset URLs change.~~ |  |  | Cancelled |  |  |\n| DMU-011 | Data Migration | The system will support a snapshot and delta migration approach: an initial bulk data export followed by one or more delta migrations based on timestamps, and a final delta run close to DNS cutover to minimise data gaps. | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-011> |\n| DMU-012 | Data Migration | The system will be supported by repeatable migration scripts capable of executing multiple delta runs; one-off scripts that cannot be re-executed will not be acceptable. | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-012> |\n| DMU-013 | URL Strategy | The system will preserve the existing storefront locale prefix conventions: AU (root, no prefix), US (/us/), UK (/uk/), EU (/en-eu/, /fr-eu/, /es-eu/, /it-eu/), HK (/hk/), ME (/en-ae/), and ROW (/en-ch/, /en-ca/). | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-013> |\n| DMU-014 | URL Strategy | The system will update category URLs to support SEO consolidation and reduce category cannibalisation (e.g. a canonical path such as /clothing/dresses), with 301 redirects applied from all legacy category URLs. | Accenture | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-014> |\n| DMU-015 | URL Strategy | The system will preserve the existing product URL format including the .html suffix (e.g. /alchemy-ruffle-mini-dress-blue-poppy.html) to maintain existing indexed URLs and avoid unnecessary 301 overhead. | Accenture | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-015> |\n| DMU-016 | URL Strategy | The system will configure the AU storefront as the root domain with no locale prefix and designate it as the x-default hreflang target. | Accenture | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-016> |\n| DMU-017 |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| DMU-018 | URL Strategy | The system will implement 301 permanent redirects for all URLs that change as a result of the platform migration, covering product, category, content, and asset pages. | Accenture | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-018> |\n| DMU-019 | URL Strategy | The system will implement all URL redirects as defined in the redirect mapping document, which will be produced during the build phase and validated prior to go-live. | Accenture | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-019> |\n| DMU-020 | URL Strategy | The system will manage all 301 redirects at the CDN or edge level to minimise performance impact on the application layer. |  | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-020> |\n| DMU-021 | URL Strategy | The system will preserve all existing CDN redirect rules and SEO configuration from the current Cloudflare setup, carrying them forward to the new platform CDN during migration. | Zimmermann | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-021> |\n| DMU-022 | SEO | The system will output canonical tags on all indexable pages, referencing the preferred URL for that storefront. | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-022> |\n| DMU-023 | SEO | The system will apply canonical tags on all filtered and faceted PLP URLs pointing back to the unfiltered base PLP URL to prevent duplicate content indexation. | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed | We would like to control updating the canonical as needed on indexible filter pages | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-023> |\n| DMU-024 | SEO | The system will apply hreflang tags only on canonical PDP URLs; non-canonical URL variants will not carry hreflang tags, and canonical tags will be retained on all PDP URL variants. | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-024> |\n| DMU-025 | SEO | The system will implement hreflang tags on all pages via XML sitemap format, mapping all locale codes to their respective storefront URLs. | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-025> |\n| DMU-026 | SEO | The system will consolidate hreflang tags from the current 200+ country-specific tags to approximately 12 regional and language-level tags, to be confirmed with the Sparro SEO team prior to implementation. | Tell No Lies | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-026> |\n| DMU-027 | SEO | The system will automatically generate and serve XML sitemaps per storefront and locale, refreshed on a scheduled daily basis. | Accenture | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-027> |\n| DMU-028 | SEO | The system will exclude disabled and deleted pages from all XML sitemaps upon regeneration. | Accenture | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-028> |\n| DMU-029 | SEO | The system will ensure homepage URLs in XML sitemaps include a trailing slash. | Accenture | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-029> |\n| DMU-030 | SEO | The system will ensure that all URLs blocked in robots.txt do not appear in any XML sitemap. | Accenture | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-030> |\n| DMU-031 | SEO | The system will render all product, category, and content pages server-side (SSR) to ensure full crawlability by search engines and AI bots without dependence on client-side JavaScript execution. | Accenture | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-031> |\n| DMU-032 | SEO | The system will generate unique, human-readable title tags per page following the existing format: [Product Name] [Colour] ~~Online~~ | Zimmermann, configurable via Business Manager meta tag rules. | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-032> |\n| DMU-033 | SEO | The system will generate unique meta description tags per product and category page, sourced from product and catalogue data in SFCC. | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-033> |\n| DMU-034 | SEO | The system will implement a single H1 tag per page template across homepage, PLP, and PDP, with correct H2–H6 heading hierarchy and no duplicate heading tags. | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-034> |\n| DMU-035 | SEO | The system will include the product colour within the H1 tag on all PDP pages. | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-035> |\n| DMU-036 | SEO | The system will provide a CMS-editable on-page SEO content field on all category and PLP pages, configurable at individual storefront level. |  |  | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-036> |\n| DMU-037 | SEO | The system will serve a robots.txt file that permits crawling of all indexable pages including the bag page, and restricts crawling of checkout flow steps, account pages, search result pages, and filtered URL parameters. | Accenture | Config | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-037> |\n| DMU-038 | SEO | The system will implement Product and Merchant Listing Schema on all PDPs per the schema template provided by the Tell No Lies SEO team. | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-038> |\n| DMU-039 | SEO | The system will implement CollectionPage, BreadcrumbList, and ItemList Schema on all PLP pages per the Sparro SEO team schema template. | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-039> |\n| DMU-040 | SEO | The system will implement LocalBusiness Schema on all individual boutique location detail pages per the Sparro SEO team schema template. | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-040> |\n| DMU-041 | SEO | The system will implement Organisation Schema on each regional storefront homepage per the Sparro SEO team schema template, with url and contactPoint fields configured per storefront. | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-041> |\n| DMU-042 | SEO | The system will implement structured data for products to include available sizes and per-offer availability, driven by real-time inventory data. | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-042> |\n| DMU-043 | GEO | The system will deliver the technical foundations required for post-launch GEO enablement — including SSR, structured data, canonical URLs, and XML sitemaps — ensuring no architectural decisions block future GEO activation. | Accenture | Custom | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-043> |\n| DMU-044 | Data Migration | The system will migrate customer wishlist data from Magento, mapping wishlist items to the corresponding SFCC product records and associating them with the migrated customer account via Omneo ID. | Accenture |  | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-044> |\n| DMU-045 | Data Migration | The system will migrate product enrichment data currently maintained in Magento to SFCC, including badges, category assignments, colour swatches, colour grouping, swatch images and Shop the Look associations, mapped to the corresponding SFCC product and catalogue structure. | Accenture |  | Confirmed | Shop the Look - Logic | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-045> |\n|  | Data Migration | The system will migrate active Notify Me subscriptions from Magento to SFCC, carrying forward customer email addresses and product IDs and mapping them to the corresponding SFCC product records. | Accenture |  | Confirmed |  | <https://zimmermannworkboard.atlassian.net/issues/?jql=project%20%3D%20%22SFCC%22%20AND%20labels%20%3D%20DMU-046> |",
      "format": "markdown"
    },
    "emoji": "1f4c4",
    "page_width": "max"
  }
}"}

